Don't report a directory as removed by rm -v when it was left in place.
When an entry in a directory could not be removed, remove_file()
rightly skipped the rmdir(), but with -v it still printed "removed
directory: 'DIR'", for that directory and for each one above it, though
all of them remained. Print the message only when the directory has
actually been removed.

---
 libbb/remove_file.c |    2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/libbb/remove_file.c
+++ b/libbb/remove_file.c
@@ -74,7 +74,7 @@
 			return -1;
 		}
 
-		if (flags & FILEUTILS_VERBOSE) {
+		if (status == 0 && (flags & FILEUTILS_VERBOSE)) {
 			printf("removed directory: '%s'\n", path);
 		}
 
